course: dictionary
lesson: 4634
title: Hindi and words from Hindi
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hindi is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter, like France or English. It is the name of one of the main languages of India, spoken by hundreds of millions of people. «Priya's grandma in Leicester smiles: "Pyjamas, shampoo and bungalow are Hindi words, beta!"» Beta is a loving word for a child, so the clue tells you the grandma is speaking about a language she knows well.
explain: Hindi can also be an adjective, a word that describes a noun. In «a Hindi film», Hindi tells you the film is in or about the Hindi language. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
explain: Hindi has also given English many words during British rule in India. «Pyjamas» came from Hindi and Urdu, «shampoo» first meant press or massage, and «bungalow» means a house in the Bengal style. «Jungle» came from Hindi «jangal», meaning wild land.
fact: Hindi is one of the main languages of India, spoken by hundreds of millions of people.
fact: Hindi is written in the Devanagari script.
fact: «Hindi» as an adjective means in or about the Hindi language, as in «a Hindi film».
fact: «Jungle» came from Hindi «jangal», meaning wild land.
fact: English and Hindi both belong to the Indo-European family, but Mandarin Chinese belongs to a different family.
exercise: What is Hindi? | *A language of India, spoken by hundreds of millions of people | A country in Africa | A kind of food from Leicester | A plant that grows in the jungle
exercise: In «a Hindi film», what does Hindi tell you? | *The film is in or about the Hindi language | The film is shown only on a Monday | The film is very old | The film is about a jungle
exercise: Which English word came from Hindi «jangal», meaning wild land? | bicycle | *jungle | window | castle
test: English and Hindi both belong to which language family? | Mandarin Chinese family | Hindi has no family at all | The jungle family | *Indo-European
test: The English word «shampoo» first meant what? | A house in the Bengal style | Stolen goods | A bubbly drink | *Press or massage
exam: Which statement is true? | Hindi is spoken only by a few hundred people in one valley | *Hindi is written in the Devanagari script | Hindi has no written form at all | Hindi is written in Chinese characters
